---
system: sys-19-billing-subscription
flow_id: checkout-initiate-mobile
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/19-billing-subscription#post-v1billingcheckout-session
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, BillingService, Stripe, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - POST /v1/billing/checkout-session
  - GET /v1/billing/orders/{order_id}
externals: [Stripe]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - parent_jwt_stale_re_pin_required
  - sku_not_found
  - stripe_unavailable
  - payment_method_declined
  - duplicate_order_in_flight
  - fraud_check_held
idempotency: X-Request-Id dedup over 24h; replay on completed checkout returns existing order
retry: caller-side exponential backoff on 5xx only
timeout: 5s p99 for POST; checkout completion is async
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant BillingService
    participant Stripe
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp: parent in pr_checkout taps "Confirm purchase"
    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/billing/checkout-session {sku_id, quantity, billing_address, X-Request-Id} and parent JWT Bearer
    Gateway->>Gateway: auth-resolver — JWT audience: tbot:parent (sys-17)
    alt parent_jwt_stale_re_pin_required
        Note over Gateway: parent JWT issued > 60s ago (ADR-0005 D6)
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 401 parent_jwt_stale — re-PIN required
    else authenticated
        Gateway->>BillingService: forward request
        BillingService->>BillingService: verify parent JWT freshness < 60s (ADR-0005 D6)
        alt duplicate_order_in_flight
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT orders WHERE x_request_id=? AND state NOT IN ('cancelled','failed')
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: existing order row
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {order_id, stripe_checkout_url, expires_at} (existing)
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200 (idempotent replay)
        else sku_not_found
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT skus WHERE id=?
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: no rows
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 404 sku_not_found
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 404
        else fraud_check_held
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT orders {sku_id, quantity, billing_address, state: 'fraud_review', x_request_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: order_id
            Note over BillingService: fraud rule triggered — order held, ops notified async
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 202 {order_id, state: 'fraud_review'}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 202
        else stripe_unavailable
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT orders {sku_id, quantity, billing_address, state: 'created', x_request_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: order_id
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/checkout/sessions {line_items, success_url, cancel_url, metadata.order_id}
            Stripe--xBillingService: 5xx / timeout
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE orders SET state='failed' WHERE id=order_id
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 502 stripe_unavailable
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 502
        else success
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT orders {sku_id, quantity, billing_address, state: 'created', x_request_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: order_id
            BillingService->>Stripe: POST /v1/checkout/sessions {line_items, success_url, cancel_url, metadata.order_id}
            Stripe-->>BillingService: {id: cs_..., url: stripe_checkout_url, expires_at}
            BillingService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE orders SET stripe_checkout_session_id=cs_..., state='pending_payment'
            BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {order_id, stripe_checkout_url, expires_at}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp: presents Stripe-hosted checkout in webview / SDK redirect
    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: payment completion is async — see stripe-webhook-processing.sequence.mmd, orders.state transitions to 'paid' via webhook worker
    loop poll until state='paid' or expires_at exceeded
        ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/billing/orders/{order_id} and parent JWT Bearer
        Gateway->>BillingService: forward
        BillingService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT orders WHERE id=?
        PostgreSQL-->>BillingService: {state, ...}
        BillingService-->>Gateway: 200 {order_id, state, ...}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end
    Note over ParentApp: state='paid' → advance to pr_confirm screen

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 5s p99 for POST — checkout async — X-Request-Id 24h dedup — exp backoff on 5xx only
